# EdgeOne Pages response headers for STATIC assets (index.html, chat.html,
# reset-password.html, blogs/newsletter). Pages Functions set their own headers
# from the Response (see functions/middleware.js jsonResponse), so this file only
# governs the static HTML.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: a <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy"> can set
# object-src / base-uri / form-action, but browsers IGNORE frame-ancestors,
# X-Frame-Options and Strict-Transport-Security in a <meta>. Those must be real
# response headers. chat.html holds an authenticated session, so it must never be
# framable (clickjacking) — hence frame-ancestors 'none' + X-Frame-Options: DENY.
#
# NOTE: the CSP here intentionally has NO script-src/default-src. The pages use
# inline scripts and inline event handlers, so a script-src would break them.
# We only tighten the directives that don't require refactoring the pages.
#
# DEPLOY VERIFY: after upload, run
#   curl -sI https://econintel.edgeone.app/chat.html | grep -i -E 'frame|strict-transport|content-security'
# and confirm the headers appear. If EdgeOne does not honour _headers, set the
# same headers as Rules in the EdgeOne dashboard instead.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
